=== CI feedback (PR #78, first push, commit e5fd460): 3 jobs failed (delivery-activation, rccad-methodology, validation-closure) ===
root cause: these jobs run the full 'ocor-runtime/tests/' sweep against a real, ephemeral PostgreSQL service container, but provisioned no TypeDB service; test_ocor_dev_0017.py's typedb_reachable fixture correctly failed closed (pytest.fail, not a skip) rather than silently passing without a real backend -- exactly the mandate's non-negotiable behavior, but it exposed that TypeDB was never wired into CI the way PostgreSQL already is.
fix (root cause, not a workaround): added a real, ephemeral TypeDB service container (same pinned image digest as deploy/bootstrap/compose.yaml) to the 3 affected workflows (.github/workflows/ocor-delivery-activation.yml, ocor-rccad.yml, ocor-validation-closure.yml), mirroring the existing postgres service pattern exactly. Also hardened spikes/typedb_exact_commit/adapter.py's initialize() to create the ocor_default database if absent (check-before-mutate, same pattern as deploy/bootstrap/init/initialize_services.py's step_graph_databases) -- the ocor-bootstrap stack's persistent database already existed locally, but a fresh CI-provisioned TypeDB instance has none.

=== verification of the database check-before-create logic against a real, throwaway scratch database (never touching the shared ocor_default database) ===
GET /v1/databases before: scratch-probe-db absent
POST /v1/databases/scratch-probe-db: HTTP 200 (created)
GET /v1/databases after create: scratch-probe-db present
DELETE /v1/databases/scratch-probe-db: HTTP 200
GET /v1/databases after delete: scratch-probe-db absent, ocor_default still present (untouched)

